  "notes": "{挿|さ}す means to insert or put something into an opening, slot, or container.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle for the object being inserted\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {花|はな}を{花瓶|かびん}に{挿|さ}す: to put flowers in a vase\n- {鍵|かぎ}を{挿|さ}す: to insert a key\n- コンセントを{挿|さ}す: to plug in\n- {髪|かみ}に{挿|さ}す: to put (ornament) in one's hair\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {挿|さ}し{木|き}: plant cutting (for propagation)\n- {挿|さ}し{絵|え}: illustration (inserted in text)\n\nKANJI DISTINCTION:\nSeveral verbs read さす use different kanji:\n- {挿|さ}す: to insert\n- {刺|さ}す: to stab, pierce\n- {指|さ}す: to point\n- {差|さ}す: to hold up (umbrella)\n- {射|さ}す: (light) to shine",
